    "Scouting Notes": "Likely Multi Inning Reliever\n High K BB% doesn't match the early mediocre results he has gotten in the ACL.\n Fastball is upper 92 94 but can touch 96\n Stuff and mechanics are quite reminiscent of Freddy Peralta at that age/level.\n Based on small amount of video available, appears to have a high VAA (Vertical Attack Angle). Should get a lot of whiffs on high FB.\n Fastball appears to cut at times, might just be the camera angle on sliders.\n Slider looks sharp, with late break, I think there's a curveball too, though they might be blending at times?\n Has some feel for changeup.\n Walks were much higher his first season of pro ball. Is the improvement legit, or will it fall off in Low A?\n One to follow. Could be an arm that flies up my rankings by the end of the year with a good showing in Carolina.",
